 <iati-activity default-currency="EUR" hierarchy="2" humanitarian="0" iati-activities:version="2.02" xml:lang="EN" xmlns:iati-activities="http://d-portal.org/xmlns/iati-activities" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <iati-identifier>NL-KVK-40409352-PRJ13-169-0003</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="NL-KVK-40409352" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands Red Cross</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CEA Boost project Mali</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Engagement and Accountability (CEA) strengthening of the Mali Red Cross.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kayes region, Mali</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Setting up a feedback mechanism is one of the key pillars of community engagement that can help the MRC to be more accountable to beneficiaries, partners and donors, and it contributes to better quality of programmes. A feedback mechanism should be integrated into all programmes run by a National Society, and the MRC is starting the process, having a validated CoC, internal regulation, a CEA strategy in place and a CEA/PGI focal point in place.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Targeted communities under Chronic Crisis project.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The process is new and has to be supported to be able to be included in all the Project Management Cycle of all the projects, but with our support we are able to start the process with the branch of Kayes and the project Chronic Crisis. All the PNS are also active to include the feedback mechanisms in the projects they support in other branches.</narrative>
  </description>
